  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Alpha hydrogen&nbsp;in aldehydes&nbsp;are slightly acidic and in presence of alkali they release&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>ions and carbanion.</p><p>Ethyl bromide undergoes nucleophilic substitution reaction with the carbanion generated, where bromide nucleophile&nbsp;is replaced by the carbanion&nbsp;to form ketone by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;mechansim</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0059_298b306cd09b.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 270px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
